      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0027" n="art0027">
        <p>BEFORE THE MAGISTRATES.</p>
        <p>ALLEGED EMBEZZLEMENT.</p>
        <p>At the Warrington Occasional Court, on Saturday, Edward Farley, carter, of Stockton Resta, was charged with o:nbezzling the sum of £1 55.. belonging to his employers, Messrs. W. White and Son, Ltd., mineral water manufacturers, Stockton Heath. Mr. Browne appeared to prosecute.-.-14:ViderICO WAS given to the 'sfect that Farley. on March Ist, sold some mineral `Qlters to a person on his round and received £1 ss. in Llaont for them. On his return he did not account Since Money, his books showing that it was owing. and tben be had been pressed about it several times roun,eveatnally, when a fresh carter was put on the it Was found that the money bad been paid When the Mineral waters were delivered. Farley was remanded to the Petty Sessions, to be held at Stockton Heath on Tuesday next. EXTECNS EVE Tif EFTS FROM THE RAILWAY. George Green, Knutsford-road ; George Latham, Bennett-street, and Joseph Fellows, Longford-street, st were charged at the Police Court, on Saturday, with 7- stealing a case containing 24 bottles of stout, value Ss., the property of the L. and N.-W. Railway Company, eotn a van in Dallarn-lane siding. Superintendent Monaghan stated that the case was put into the van, packed, and seen safe, about nine o'clock. green Was employed in a, hut in the ballam siding, as a checker. Detective Coward w`ls passing the 'hit. and looked through the window, ~and saw Green an .1 Latham trying to open a lock on the van. He asked them what they were doing, and they - said they were trying to get, it open. The detective Drought them to the Police Station,where they admitted ltealing 24 bottles of stout, and also made a statement I:4lPlicating the prisoner Follows. who admitted receiv. It'lK eight bottles of stout. Daring the last 12 months s railway company had lost al) mt 1,0n3 bottles of ‘ZPIIt, and all along Green had been suspected.Pr:soners "resent to gaol for a month.</p>
      </div>
