      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0143" n="art0143">
        <head>SIGNALMAN'S TRIALS. -- -- Constipation and Piles for Two Years.</head>
        <p>A SIGNALMAN'S TRIALS. -- -- Constipation and Piles for Two Years.</p>
        <p>CURED BY BILE BEANS.</p>
        <p>Everyone knows how exacting and responsible are the duties of amtilway signalman. On his clear-headedness and quickness depend the safety of thousands of lives, and it is a very serious matter when a pointsman loses his health. Mr. W. Henry Owens is a signalman on the L. &amp; N. W. Railway, and lives an Padeswood, near Mold, Flintshire. An alert, intelligent, middle-aged man, Mr. Qwens has endured many trials from digestive disorders but now, thanks entirely to Bile Beans, he is enjoying the best of health. " For two years I suffered from constipation and piles," he told a representative of the " Denbighshire Free Press." "I was con- tinually having headaches and pains in my back, which /pads me feel very weak and made my work anything but a pleasure. My appetite was affected, and my bright spirits vanished. Though I tried all sorts of medicine nothing afforded ma more than temporary relief. "Then I gave Bile Beans a triel. and I soon felt better. After a regular course of Bile Beans, I could go through my day's work with ease and pleasure. My spirits were brighter, and my appetite was greatly improved. Now I feel that Bile Beans have effected a complete and permanentcure." Bile Beans are the world's greatest remedy for all digestive ills. Refuse all substitutes and accept only Bile Beans for Billionsness. Sold only in sealed boxes, at Is. ltd. or `2s. 9d. per box.</p>
        <p>.-..----mielo•--•••••-</p>
        <p>A COSTLY SEWERAGE SCHEME.</p>
        <p>The Chairman of the St. Heleins Health Comtnittte on Wednesdny submitted to the( Town Council a pro- positiL n that a new sewerage scheme should be provided for the Parr and Sutton districts at an estimated cost of 5:49,000. He pointed out thst the Committee had been making investigations for the past ten years, and they thought the scheme they recommended was the best possible one. The scheme was adopted.</p>
      </div>
