      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0162" n="art0162">
        <head>Duck and Green Peas.</head>
        <p>Duck and Green Peas.</p>
        <p>More than one famous cycling hostelry has built up a great reputation on duck and green peas. There is one tiny but celebrated inn in Hertford- shire which stands alone at the summit of a hill. It is rumoured that in Certain months of the year no traveller/ on foot or bieycle has ever been known to pass that house without calling- for refreshment, so steep is the hill and so good the entertainment.</p>
        <p>But the chief attraction to cyclists was on Sundays during the season when mine host served his famous dinner of duck and green peas, when his table was always crowded with cyclists, and many who had travelled out on dining thoughts intent, were turned empty away simply because of lack of accommodation.</p>
        <p>By the side of the inn was the pond in , which swam all the week scores of ducks of every hue till they were hauled out on Saturday night to make Sunday's cycling feast. Having been disappointed of dinner on one occasion a party of cyclists set out to discover other rural inns with duck-ponds,, with. the result that we nave new in Hertfordshire, to this writer's knowledge, at least twenty inns where a special cyclists dinner of duck and green peas is served on Sundays during the season. If you are in Herts during the next three or four weeks try to dine at the inn by the side of the duck-pond. That 's where they serve the duck and green peas.</p>
