      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0200" n="art0200">
        <head>WARRINGTONIANS IN PARIS.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTONIANS IN PARIS.</p>
        <p>Some 25 members of the Junior C)nservative Club ventured far afield last week-end, when they visited Paris. Under the guidance of Mr. Herbert Hayes, they loft Warrington on Saturday morning, and in Man- chester joined the 700 members of the Nelson Co-opera- tive Society. The members of the club reached War- rington on Monday morning, having seen many interest- ing sights in the gay city. The visitors were received at the Elyse° by Pbasident Fallieres, the, reception having been arranged by the British Embassy at the request of the society. Paris was reached at eight o'clock on Sunday morning, and the return journey to England was commenced at 9.5 pan. the same day. The journey was somewhat fatiguing, but the party thoroughly enjoyed themselves. - CHILDREN'S TREAT AT FEARNHEAD.</p>
        <p>On Whit Monday afternoon at Fearnhead the children of Padgate, Fearnhead and Houghton Green were, through the generosity and kindness of Mr. George Mather (the District Councillor) Mrs. Mather, and other friends, given a treat. Gaines and amusements were entered into heartily by the youngsters in a field adjoining Mr. Mather residence, whilst during the afternoon sweet music was discoursed by the band from. the Padgate industrial School. At the end of the day bags containing oranges. &amp;c., were given to the children who of course, highly appreciate the gift. This treat is an annual affair in addition to the usual Walking Day and is naturally looked forward to by the children of the various districts participating.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-06-09_WidnesExaminer_art0201" n="art0201">
